
Problem Statement: Bank Account Management System


Objective

Write an object-oriented Java program to implement a basic Bank Account Management System. The program must define a standard class structure to handle account initialization, deposit, withdrawal operations, and displaying account information using separate object methods.

Requirements

1. Class Design (BankAccount)
Create a class named BankAccount containing the following components:
• Data Members (Fields):
	• accountNumber (String or numeric type)
	• accountHolderName (String)
	• balance (double)
• Constructor:
	• A parameterized constructor that accepts inputs for all three data members and initializes the object's account details.
• Methods:
	• deposit(double amount): Adds the given amount to the current balance.
	• withdraw(double amount): Deducts the given amount from the balance only if the account has a sufficient balance.
	• checkBalance(): Returns the current balance value.
	• displayAccount(): Prints all the account details (Account Number, Holder Name, and Balance) to the console.
2. Execution Logic (main method)
Inside the Main execution class, implement the following sequential steps:
1. Read the account details (accountNumber, accountHolderName) and the initialBalance from the standard user input.
2. Instantiate a BankAccount object by passing these initial inputs into the parameterized constructor.
3. Read a deposit amount from the user and call the deposit() method.
4. Read a withdrawal amount from the user and call the withdraw() method.
5. Call the displayAccount() method to output the final account details and updated balance.

Constraints

• All balance modifications (depositing and withdrawing) must be processed through their respective class methods. Do not calculate or change the balance variables directly within the main() method.
• A withdrawal should only succeed if the withdrawal amount is less than or equal to the active balance.
